## One important architectural decision

I recommend keeping these responsibilities separate:

| Service                 | Responsibility                                         |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Firebase Authentication | Google account sign-in                                 |
| Firestore               | Users, roles, identities metadata, logs, notifications |
| Gemini                  | AI assistant and security summaries                    |
| Python FastAPI          | Actual biometric processing                            |
| PostgreSQL              | Encrypted biometric templates and backend records      |

**Do not migrate encrypted biometric templates into Firestore just to make the architecture look unified.** Your existing backend has a specific encryption and persistence design that should be preserved.

Also, your current project is a research prototype: it does not yet have real-data validation, liveness detection, or production-grade biometric authorization. The prompt deliberately prevents Gemini from inventing these capabilities.

